  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Isiolo Drought Response and Recovery Project; Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">After the devastating drought of 2016/17 and the emergency response in Isiolo County the community is still vulnerable and there is need for continuous support to make sure that they recover and their resilience is strengthened to enable them cope with future droughts. The long rains did not help as they were poorly distributed. As the long rains season ended, many parts of the ASALs are still experiencing a severe deficit in vegetation condition, lengthy distances to water, unusually high food prices, and worrying levels of malnutrition. This has led to conflict over the scarce resources. The level of recovery in rangeland conditions and livestock productivity has not been sufficient to see families through the on going dry period. No crop harvest is expected due to poor performance of the long rains. This project will complement the work of other actors in areas of WASH, Food security(animal&amp; livestock production), Nutrition and Peace &amp; security.</narrative>
  </description>
